  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:al_yashov_dakh">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/74/21"/><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/1"/>Let the oppressed not be put to shame,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/2"/>let the poor and needy praise Your Name.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/22/12"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/3"/>Be not far [removed] from us,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/4"/>for distress is near,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/5"/>and there is no one to help.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/6"/>For I will pardon their iniquity,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/7"/>and their sin I will no longer mention.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/8"/>Pardon Your people
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/9"/>that have sinned before You,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/10"/>and all their transgressions
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/11"/>that they have transgressed unto You,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/12"/>and grant mercy
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/13"/>before their captors.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/14"/>And You, God that pardons,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/15"/>Gracious, Merciful, Slow to anger,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/16"/>and Abounding in kindness—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_yashov_dakh/17"/>do not forsake them.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
